  {
   "evidence": "Only `doubletAction`/`singletAction` are defined (lines 64, 82), both fixed to `Fin 2` resp. the trivial isospin; there is no general-representation statement in the file.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/PVES/Electroweak/ElectricCharge.lean",
   "fix": "Qualify the sentence, e.g. \"So for the doublets and singlets treated here the electric charge of a state with weak-isospin third component `T\u00b3` and hypercharge `Y` is `Q = T\u00b3 + Y / 2`.\"",
   "issue": "The module docstring concludes \"the electric charge of a state with weak-isospin third component `T\u00b3` and hypercharge `Y` is `Q = T\u00b3 + Y / 2`\", phrased for an arbitrary state. The file only establishes the doublet case (`doubletAction_chargeGenerator`, `isospinT3_add_mulVec_single`, both over `Fin 2`) and the singlet case (`singletAction_chargeGenerator`); no other weak-isospin representation appears.",
   "line": 27
  },
  {
   "evidence": "`chargeGenerator = (\u27e8I \u2022 isospinT3, _\u27e9, 1)` (line 124) and `doubletAction_chargeGenerator : doubletAction y chargeGenerator = I \u2022 (isospinT3 + ((y / 2 : \u211d) : \u2102) \u2022 1)` (line 152) \u2014 the relation is operator multiplication by `-i`, not a form.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/PVES/Electroweak/ElectricCharge.lean",
   "fix": "Reword to \"whose associated Hermitian generator, `-i` times its action, is `T\u00b3 + Y / 2`\" (which is what `doubletAction_chargeGenerator` delivers).",
   "issue": "`chargeGenerator`'s docstring says \"whose Hermitian form is `T\u00b3 + Y / 2`\". \"Hermitian form\" is the standard name for a sesquilinear form, not for the Hermitian operator obtained by stripping the `i` from an anti-Hermitian generator; the docstring means the latter.",
   "line": 122
  }
 ],
